  "configuration_id": "config_037",
  "reason": "The current best is config_039 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, ViT-L, transformer, weighted) at 0.725 acc. Evidence strongly supports scvi_n200 as the best RNA encoder, ViT-L as the best image encoder, multiprofile, and weighted fusion. The only remaining uncertainty among the top-tier configurations is the aggregation method in the multimodal setting: transformer (0.725) vs. avgpool. In the RNA-only setting, the gap was negligible (0.653 vs. 0.650), so the multimodal interaction could theoretically shift this. Config_037 (avgpool, weighted) is the single closest untested variant to the current best, changing only aggregation. As the final experiment, it offers the highest (albeit small) probability of exceeding 0.725 while also confirming whether the transformer aggregation's marginal edge in RNA-only carries over to multimodal fusion. All other untested options involve downgrading the RNA encoder (scgpt/PCA) or image encoder (ResNet50), which the evidence strongly indicates would underperform."
}

